  "question": {
    "text": "If the equation of the plane that contains the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and is perpendicular to each of the planes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>97</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>",
